## Start with the workflow

Most AI projects stall because they begin with a tool shortlist. The clearer path is to name one repetitive, error-prone process and map who touches it, what data moves, and where handoffs break.

## Clarity is a team habit

Operational clarity is not a dashboard. It is a shared language for decisions, owners, and evidence. When that language exists, automation becomes an obvious next step instead of a speculative upgrade.

## What Bluebook looks for

- A process that already happens every week
- Messages, documents, or approvals that scatter context
- A measurable cost: time, rework, or missed follow-up

> If you can describe the friction in one paragraph, you are ready for a workflow review. [Contact Bluebook](/en/contact/).
